DOS-PORT (patch 0118, Phase 11 iter K). Fix the slot 0111 emit-block
ordering bug that produced negative `visit_overhead_per_tile_us` in
every block under MDS_TFG_INSTR=1.

Root cause:
  Slot 0111 emit block reads `g_mds_tilemap_fg_idx` +
  `g_mds_tilemap_fg_samples[]` to compute mds_fg_total_ms (the parent
  W22.5 bracket total, used to derive iter_overhead_ms = mds_fg_-
  total_ms - dt_ms). But the original slot 0111 emit ran AFTER the
  W22.5 sample-array reset cluster — which zeros g_mds_tilemap_fg_idx
  every audit-flush. So the slot 0111 sum was always 0 →
  iter_overhead_ms = 0 - dt_ms = NEGATIVE → visit_overhead_per_-
  tile_us NEGATIVE every block.

Symptom in iter J (real-HW PODP-OD-83):
  visit_overhead_per_tile_us = -58.03 µs / tile (load-bearing — should
                               be positive iteration overhead)
Smoke baseline pre-fix:
  visit_overhead_per_tile_us = -1.26 µs / tile (smaller magnitude only
                               because smoke was minimal-scene with
                               few drawn tiles)

Fix:
  Snapshot mds_fg_total_ms BEFORE the W22.5 reset cluster, store in
  file-scope `g_slot_0118_mds_fg_total_ms_snapshot` (double; declared
  in Utils/diagnostic_timers.h alongside the slot 0111 storage cluster).
  Slot 0111 emit block consumes the snapshot via the same name.
  Snapshot is reset to 0.0 at end-of-audit-flush alongside the slot
  0111 11-counter reset cluster (defensive lifetime discipline; the
  snapshot is overwritten unconditionally at next audit-flush entry).

Code surface (~25 lines net change):
  Utils/diagnostic_timers.h:
    extern decl `extern double g_slot_0118_mds_fg_total_ms_snapshot;`
    alongside slot 0111's g_mds_tfg_* externs.
  Renderer.cpp:
    - Storage definition `double g_slot_0118_mds_fg_total_ms_snapshot
      = 0.0;` alongside the slot 0111 storage cluster.
    - Snapshot computation block at the W22.5 reset site (gated on
      _abl_mds_tfg_instr() — no cost when env unset; identical
      6-line loop body to original slot 0111 compute, just earlier
      in the function).
    - Slot 0111 emit block's mds_fg_total_ms initializer changed
      from inline-compute-from-samples to
      `g_slot_0118_mds_fg_total_ms_snapshot`.
    - End-of-block reset of snapshot alongside slot 0111 counter
      reset.

Why file-scope-static instead of function-scope local:
  The slot 0111 emit lives 4 if-blocks deeper in
  _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit. A function-scope local would be
  in scope but the patch surface is cleaner with a named file-scope
  variable that mirrors the slot 0111 storage discipline. Single-
  writer (this function); no concurrency. Minimal extra storage
  footprint (8 bytes).

Self-checks preserved (per slot 0111 contract § 6):
  - tiles_visited == drawn_normal + drawn_special + skipped_attr +
    skipped_oob (instrumentation drift check) — unaffected by this
    fix; the bug was downstream in the derived metrics layer.
  - drawtile_count + drawsprite_count == drawn_normal +
    drawn_special — unaffected.

Expected iter K-1 emit (PLAY1, real-HW, drawTileFast=ON):
  drawtile_per_us drops from ~58.0 µs (iter J) toward
  blit_indexed_per_us (~25.7 µs iter J)
  dispatch_overhead_per_tile_us drops from ~32.4 µs toward 0
  visit_overhead_per_tile_us NOW POSITIVE (iteration loop overhead;
  expected ~5-15 µs / tile per FPS-DEEPDIVE Cand #5 H3 hypothesis
  if iter-loop is significant; could also be near-zero if H1 / H2
  outcomes dominate)

Per pressure_test_tidy_narratives.md: this is a measurement-bug fix,
not a perf lever. No fps gain comes from this patch alone. Iter K-1
must still measure the slot 0117 lever's contribution. The
visit_overhead_per_tile_us going from negative to positive is a
sanity check that the instrumentation is now self-consistent —
flush-instr can use it to discriminate which of H1/H2/H3 (or
combination) dominates the residual mds_tilemap_fg cost after
slot 0117.

